+## Live agent lifecycle (`live-agents`)
+
+`ci/run live-agents --plugin=aicliagents` runs the plugin's
+`tests/live/agent_lifecycle.sh` ON `.4` (through the host guard, exit 37 on a
+wrong host) against the deployed plugin. For every agent in `AgentRegistry` it
+installs the agent through the Store's `install_agent` action when it is absent,
+checks that the binary runs and that `versions.json` and the Store agree,
+upgrades it (or downgrades it and restores it), tears the agent mount down and
+mounts it again through the plugin's own storage seam — on a plain-directory
+agent with an empty stale mount injected first, the 2026-09-24 "[Agent Binary
+Missing]" fault — and starts and closes a throw-away `e2elive…` workspace. Every
+agent stays installed.
+
+- **In no group.** It downloads every agent, so it is not part of `all` or
+  `release-gate`. Run it after the Factory publish of the version you will release.
+- **Agents in use are never disturbed and never fail the run.** An agent with a
+  live non-e2e workspace (or an outside process running its binary) gets a WARN
+  line naming the workspaces; its install, version change and remount are SKIPPED
+  with reason `in use`; the binary check and a separate e2e workspace still run.
+  `--live-args="--include-busy"` runs the full lifecycle on them too.
+- **Pass-through flags:** `--live-args="…"` (or `CI_LIVE_ARGS`) goes to the suite:
+  `--dry-run`, `--agents=a,b`, `--include-busy`, `--skip-change`,
+  `--skip-remount`, `--skip-session`, `--no-version-check`,
+  `--install-timeout=S`, `--session-wait=S`. A dry run signs nothing.
+- **Artifact:** `runners/live-agents-report.sh` signs
+  `<plugin>/.ci-artifacts/live-agents.json` (schema `aicli-live-agents/1`) with
+  the gate key and the release gate's canonical JSON. It records the tested
+  plugin version, per-agent status, the in-use agents, and totals.
+- **Storefront requirement:** `ci/storefront` step ⓪b runs
+  `scripts/factory/live-agents-verify.php`: HMAC valid · same plugin · the run
+  tested THIS version · the whole registry ran · no FAIL · at most 7 days old
+  (`LIVE_AGENTS_MAX_AGE_DAYS`). In-use skips print as a warning ("N agents not
+  re-tested because they were in use"), not a blocker. A failure stops
+  `--push` with exit **57** (`--force` downgrades it to a warning, with the
+  user's explicit consent only); a dry run only warns.
+
